Check the units of measure for transects and perpendicular distances; that is a common source of error leading to such inappropriate density and abundance estimates.

On 06/07/2015 14:59, Laura Secada wrote:

> Thank you Eric. There is lot to change on the sampling design and the field protocol.
>
> At the moment we have run the first year ok with different models and differnt truncation values but for the second and third year we have got a density of 0.001 ind/ha and abundance of 7 which is less than N. observations. We think there might be an error in data entry or something we are doing wrong at some point.
>
> thank you,
> Laura
>
>
