> > >
> > > I understand field procedures have to be improved, but in reality we see more animals near (within 9m) from the line, but this information has been rounded to cero. What should I do? leave it that way, left truncate at some point? not include a % of cero distance data?
> > >
> > > I have tried half normal cosine, right truncation 50m, left truncation at 9m, it improves AIC (from 1937 to 1324), p values in KS test from 0.000 now gives  0.0772. gives warning on monotonicity.
> > >
> > >  Thank you for patience and time,
> > > Laura
